title: 'Gnomon boards: team analysis (Arky, Aegis, Luna, Loid, Jinx, Helix)'
summary: 'Panel found boards are spec §12.7 Doodle grown up: designed, unbuilt (kit.Canvas is a placeholder). Consensus: agents propose boards via offer slips; hybrid truth (kernel-log ops, compacted to lore-style per-node files in .paradigm/boards/ through a human export card with redaction); declarative board mods with fallbacks, no third-party JS or live iframes; structured node model so voice/gesture/VR stay open; boards never cover approval surfaces. Luna''s device: pins with author seals and a shadow that lengthens as live data goes stale. Splits: first slice (live context board vs whiteboard), renderer (Excalidraw P12 ''partial'' and stock look vs custom SVG vs React Flow), and Jinx''s two-week falsifier. Options and recommendation in .paradigm/research/gnomon-canvas/synthesis.md; awaiting founder pick.'
